      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles. Two triangles are similar if their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are proportional. In this case, the triangles are similar because they have two sides of equal length and the longest side of the larger triangle is a multiple of the longest side of the smaller triangle.\n\nGiven:\n- The side lengths of the smaller triangle are 8 cm, 8 cm, and 10 cm.\n- The longest side of the larger triangle is 25 cm.\n\nSince the triangles are similar, the ratio of the corresponding sides is the same. The ratio of the longest side of the larger triangle to the longest side of the smaller triangle is \\( \\frac{25}{10} = 2.5 \\).\n\nThis means that each side of the larger triangle is 2.5 times the corresponding side of the smaller triangle. Therefore, we can calculate the lengths of the sides of the larger triangle as follows:\n\n- The first side of the larger triangle is \\( 8 \\times 2.5 = 20 \\) cm.\n- The second side of the larger triangle is \\( 8 \\times 2.5 = 20 \\) cm.\n- The third side of the larger triangle is \\( 10 \\times 2.5 = 25 \\) cm.\n\nThe perimeter of a triangle is the sum of its side lengths. Therefore, the perimeter of the larger triangle is \\( 20 + 20 + 25 = 65 \\) cm.\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{65}\\).",
